-- 1 → 2: the `secret_sync` table of M7-L4a (docs/05 "시크릿 동기화").
--
-- The whole schema lives in `Rec.sq`; a migration is only what an installed database of the version
-- it is named after is missing. The two have to agree, and `MigrationTest` — which builds a
-- version-1 database by hand and upgrades it — is what says they do.
--
-- Never edit a migration once it has run anywhere: add the next one (docs/10 "스키마 마이그레이션").
--
-- `IF NOT EXISTS` because version 1 is not one schema. Builds between M7-L4a and its second review
-- round already had `secret_sync` in `Rec.sq` while the schema version was still 1, so a database
-- from one of those is stamped 1 and *has* the table; a plain `CREATE TABLE` would fail the upgrade
-- for exactly the devices this migration exists to rescue. The two shapes are identical, so
-- skipping the create when it is already there is the whole of the difference.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS secret_sync (
  name TEXT PRIMARY KEY, updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,
  deleted INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, dirty INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
);
